char *bc_b64_encode(const char *data, size_t len);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Encodes \f[B]len\f[R] bytes of binary \f[B]data\f[R] into a
NUL\-terminated base64 string using the standard RFC 4648 alphabet
(\f[CR]A\-Z\f[R], \f[CR]a\-z\f[R], \f[CR]0\-9\f[R], \f[CR]+\f[R],
\f[CR]/\f[R]) with \f[CR]=\f[R] padding.
.PP
The returned string is dynamically allocated and must be freed by the
caller using \f[CR]bc_free(3)\f[R].
.PP
This is a low\-level utility function used internally by the client
library for PTY data encoding (\f[CR]bc_pty_write(3)\f[R]) and other
binary payloads.
Most callers do not need to use it directly; the channel\-specific
functions handle encoding automatically.
.SH Encoding details
.IP \(bu 2
Input of 0 bytes produces an empty string (\f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
Output length is \f[CR]4 * ceil(len / 3) + 1\f[R] bytes (including NUL).
.IP \(bu 2
No line breaks are inserted (single continuous string).
.IP \(bu 2
Padding \f[CR]=\f[R] characters are appended to make the output length a
multiple of 4.
