.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The encoding uses standard base64 (not URL\-safe base64).
The \f[CR]+\f[R] and \f[CR]/\f[R] characters appear in the output and
are safe within JSON string values.
.IP \(bu 2
The function handles NUL bytes in the input correctly; the \f[B]len\f[R]
parameter determines how many bytes are encoded, not \f[CR]strlen\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
For large inputs, the output is approximately 33% larger than the input.
A 750 KB input produces approximately 1 MB of base64 output.
.IP \(bu 2
